{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-tmli-constituent-composite-agreement","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:tmli-constituent-composite-agreement","kind":"lemma","title":"Constituent and composite Markov-trace evaluations agree exactly","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-factorization","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-markov-trace-product"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-tmli-constituent-composite-agreement"],"tags":["markov-trace","iwahori-hecke","pawlei-basis","exact-identity"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_composite_agreement","text":"tmli-constituent-composite-agreement.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:tmli-constituent-composite-agreement\"></a><p><em>For a hadron <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{H} \\hookrightarrow V^{\\otimes N}</code> with\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N = 2(j_1 + \\cdots + j_n)</code> and braid word\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta_{\\mathfrak{H}} \\in B_N</code>, the constituent product\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\prod \\hat{V}_i^{\\mathrm{const}}</code> and the composite trace\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_M(\\rho(\\beta_{\\mathfrak{H}}))</code> evaluate the same element\nof <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_N(q)</code>, so</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\prod_i \\hat{V}_i^{\\mathrm{const}}\n  =\n  \\mathrm{tr}_M(\\rho(\\beta_{\\mathfrak{H}}))\n  =\n  P_{K_{\\mathfrak{H}}}(q).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tmli-constituent-composite-agreement.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"13.1.4"}
